---
title: Chocolate Chip Cookies
course: Dessert
tags: 
- Cookies
- Vegan
source: Modified from The Cookie Book
cuisine: American
servings: 24
---

Preheat an oven to 375. Lightly butter 2 #baking sheets{} or line them with parchment paper.
In a #medium bowl{}, combine the @vegan butter{125%g}, @brown sugar{100%g}(firmly packed), @sugar{100%g}, @plant-based milk{50%g}, and @vanilla extract{1%tsp} and using an #electric mixer{} on medium to high speed, cream until light and fluffy. Sift together the @all-purpose flour{220%g}, @baking powder{1%tbsp}, and @salt{1/2%tsp} and add to the butter mixture. Mix until well combined. Stir in the @vegan chocolate chips{150%g}, and optional @chopped nuts{70%g}(walnuts, pecan, or peanuts work). 

Place heaping teaspoons on the prepared baking sheets, spacing them 2 inches (5cm) apart. Bake for ~{12-15%minutes}. Allow to cool on the baking sheets for ~{5%minutes}, then transfer to #?wire racks{} to cool completely. 